WEBVTT

cue0157334
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.240
Thank you very much Susan. Ladies, gentlemen, friends. My managers was the or one of the

cue0157335
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:33.240
greatest men of his time. Usually we know my managers as a great legal mind. The only

cue0157336
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:44.959
complete code of the entire rabbinic jurisprudence was written by my managers. Every code written

cue0157337
00:00:44.959 --> 00:00:57.759
either before or after comprises a small only a small section of rabbinic law. To give you

cue0157338
00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:05.620
an example of what the code of my managers represent, it's a book containing exactly

cue0157339
00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:20.940
I counted 1,000 chapters. Each chapter has about 20 paragraphs. Every paragraph contains

cue0157340
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:30.019
between three and five legal decisions. In other words, we're talking about an individual

cue0157341
00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:41.459
who wrote, established the law in about 100,000 cases. But that was only one of the many works

cue0157342
00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:51.059
that he did. He's also known as a philosopher. As a matter of fact, they speak of my managers as a

cue0157343
00:01:51.059 --> 00:02:02.180
rationalist. And he was. He was a superb astronomer. In some of his chapters of the

cue0157344
00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:12.339
guide, my managers asked questions about the Ptolemyian astronomical system without giving

cue0157345
00:02:12.339 --> 00:02:19.380
an answer, questions that he asked in disapproval, questions that several centuries later Copernicus

cue0157346
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:30.539
would ask. Copernicus asked the same questions, but Copernicus would come to a theory that the

cue0157347
00:02:30.539 --> 00:02:38.899
earth turns around the sun. What is important is that my managers in the history of science is the

cue0157348
00:02:38.899 --> 00:02:45.899
first one who point to certain discrepancies in the Ptolemyian system. It was a great physician.

cue0157349
00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:55.740
Today, we are coming back to the medicine of my managers. They believe in three major points about

cue0157350
00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:04.619
medicine. Number one, that medicine has to be basically holistic. You cannot treat a single

cue0157351
00:03:04.619 --> 00:03:12.259
ailment of the body without taking consideration the whole environment in which the individual

cue0157352
00:03:12.259 --> 00:03:22.899
lives. He goes to such an extreme as to, as a physician, to ask a patient the color of the

cue0157353
00:03:22.899 --> 00:03:34.899
walls of his house to recommend not only medicine, but also music. A holistic concept of medicine.

cue0157354
00:03:34.899 --> 00:03:41.899
Another point which is terribly important in his medicine is the task of the doctor is not to cure,

cue0157355
00:03:41.899 --> 00:03:50.059
but to prevent the human body of becoming sick. A sick person going to a doctor is a failure of a

cue0157356
00:03:50.059 --> 00:03:59.619
doctor. The doctor should not have allowed the patient to become sick. And last but not least,

cue0157357
00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:13.740
that when the doctor applies a particular cure, he should make sure that the cure is not worse

cue0157358
00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:20.899
than the sickness itself. The implications of whatever a cure a person might have. A man of

cue0157359
00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:32.019
great mind. What I want to explore with you is an aspect of my managers which is unknown. Those

cue0157360
00:04:32.019 --> 00:04:40.459
modern scholars who have examined the Moreh Nebukhim, deal only with the rationalistic

cue0157361
00:04:40.459 --> 00:04:50.380
aspect of my managers. And indeed, he was rational. But there is something very important about my

cue0157362
00:04:50.380 --> 00:05:01.579
managers. Let me tell you first in a kernel, very briefly, what is my mind's theory of mysticism.

cue0157363
00:05:01.579 --> 00:05:09.100
And then I will try to show you how it works. The most important thing of my managers is that

cue0157364
00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:22.299
there are three stages in the human development as an individual and in humanity as an anthropological

cue0157365
00:05:22.299 --> 00:05:33.899
groups. At an early stage, humanity, or we when we are children or immature, we live in the realm

cue0157366
00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:48.540
of myth. We are mythological. We are not totally aware of either time or space. Ideas pollute our

cue0157367
00:05:48.540 --> 00:06:06.339
our mind. And those ideas prevent us from perceiving the real reality. At that stage, the

cue0157368
00:06:06.339 --> 00:06:14.820
world is anthropocentric. What I mean to say is men, the individual, the person, is at the center

cue0157369
00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:29.779
of reality. When the primitive man or we in an immature stage perceive the reality, this reality

cue0157370
00:06:29.779 --> 00:06:39.579
is a projection of ourselves. Even when we love or when we hate. Even when we speak of God, the God

cue0157371
00:06:39.739 --> 00:06:52.380
that we perceive at that early stage of development is a God fabricated by our own myth, by our own

cue0157372
00:06:52.380 --> 00:07:06.140
imagination. There is another stage. In the stage of reason, of rationality, there is a stage in which we

cue0157373
00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:18.380
discover that there is an objective reality. Something that does not depend on us. Facts. That

cue0157374
00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:34.660
there are laws, invariable, mathematical, mechanical, that did not and will not change. And then we try

cue0157375
00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:46.500
to comprehend this world. We immerse ourselves in the world of the objective. In the world of must,

cue0157376
00:07:46.500 --> 00:08:03.980
of necessity, cause, effect. But once that we course into the realm of the objective, we come at a

cue0157377
00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:16.380
boundary. And that boundary is what my mind is called the realm of the mystical. The realm of

cue0157378
00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:31.619
prophecy. There is a limit to rationality. Rationality is important, is a stage in human

cue0157379
00:08:31.619 --> 00:08:45.340
development. But there is a realm much larger and bigger and complex than the world of rationality

cue0157380
00:08:45.340 --> 00:09:05.539
that transcends it. And when you come to that border, the rules that you had while in the realm

cue0157381
00:09:05.539 --> 00:09:16.820
of rationality will no longer operate. It's a different kind of reality. For my mind it is the

cue0157382
00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:28.580
difference between the world of the mystic, in that sense, is not the world that negates rationality,

cue0157383
00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:41.179
but rather than transcends rationality. For my mind it is the Sodot, that speaks constantly. The

cue0157384
00:09:41.179 --> 00:09:54.580
secrets of the Tora. Ma'aseh Bereshit, the cosmology of the Tora. Ma'aseh Merkabah, the chariot of the

cue0157385
00:09:54.580 --> 00:10:14.020
Tora. Is not an anti-rational realm, but is the realm of the post-rational. For reasons that really are

cue0157386
00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:25.020
irrelevant at this point to explain, somehow the way God programmed the human race and the human

cue0157387
00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:37.780
individual is to evolve as an anthropological group or as an individual from the realm of the mythical,

cue0157388
00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:51.140
to the realm of the rational, to the realm of the post-rational. For my mind it is, you can never pass from the

cue0157389
00:10:51.140 --> 00:11:04.739
mythical to the post-rational. The only way to reach mysticism for my mind is, the mysticism of the Tora, the

cue0157390
00:11:04.739 --> 00:11:23.859
mysticism of the prophets, is to exhaust your rationality. And when you come to the very end of what your mind can't

cue0157391
00:11:23.859 --> 00:11:46.219
achieve, only at the border, then you could discover another realm of reality. But, for those who remain in the early stage of

cue0157392
00:11:46.219 --> 00:11:58.940
mythical thinking, the world of mysticism that they have is a figment of their own imagination. Let me be a little bit more

cue0157393
00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:12.739
articulate and precise about my mindless thinking. There are some very important ideas that my mindless discusses in

cue0157394
00:12:12.739 --> 00:12:32.099
reference to mysticism. Mysticism, for my mindless, is the aim, not of the Jew, but of the human race. It means, in different

cue0157395
00:12:32.099 --> 00:12:50.140
words, that mysticism is an anthropological dimension, is something that pertains to the very essence of humankind. That is one point,

cue0157396
00:12:50.140 --> 00:13:10.099
terribly important. Second point, the passing from the mythical to the rational, from the rational to the mystical, for my mindless, is relative to the

cue0157397
00:13:10.099 --> 00:13:33.179
human capacities. Somebody with limited education, with limited intellectual capacities, for that individual, the passing from the mythical to the rational to the

cue0157398
00:13:33.179 --> 00:13:56.580
mystical, would be different than for Sir Isaac Newton or for Dr. Albert Einstein. But nonetheless, each individual, within his or her own capacities, could develop.

cue0157399
00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:23.179
That is another aspect of this mysticism. Now, I want to be more and more specific. Briefly, the mystic is the individual who, in a sense, discovers who he or she is.

cue0157400
00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:56.539
More precise, the mystic is the one who forges him or herself. Let me explain. For the mythical mind, for the primitive, for those

cue0157401
00:14:56.539 --> 00:15:21.940
who do not face reality and rationality, to always think about some idyllic past, the paradise in the past, oh, how beautiful things were when I was a child. Always a past, a past.

cue0157402
00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:51.900
In Christian tradition, believing in Jesus in cooperation in the Corpus Christi would take us back into the time of Adam. It's the past. For the Jew, the most important aspect of time is neither the past nor the future.

cue0157403
00:15:52.900 --> 00:16:17.900
The rabbis and my monasteries emphasize, the most important moment is right now. And let me explain. What does it mean there, right now? The moment of the present.

cue0157404
00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:47.859
If we believe that there is a God who started moving things at cosmological hour zero, therefore it means that every moment now is the combination, the concatation of infinite circumstances.

cue0157405
00:16:48.900 --> 00:17:11.859
That focus all of them in this single moment. And right now you, as an individual, could do something that nobody else ever was able to do, and nobody again will ever be able to duplicate.

cue0157406
00:17:12.859 --> 00:17:29.819
And when you do that thing now, you change the course of the cosmos. And in a sense, you open new possibilities for new nows.

cue0157407
00:17:29.819 --> 00:17:56.780
The rabbis say, God never created a human being without giving he, she, gentile Jew a moment in which he, she could do something because it's in the right place at the right time.

cue0157408
00:17:56.780 --> 00:18:02.739
And because he, she has certain experience or certain knowledge or certain thing that nobody else has.

cue0157409
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:19.739
And when you grab the moment, you become something, someone that nobody else ever was like it or will be like it.

cue0157410
00:18:19.739 --> 00:18:25.699
You forge your individuality in that moment.

cue0157411
00:18:25.699 --> 00:18:55.660
There are men, humans, and they tell a story about a gentile, about an inverted sinner Jew, and about an inverted Jew.

cue0157412
00:18:55.699 --> 00:18:57.660
An executioner, a pagan executioner.

cue0157413
00:18:58.699 --> 00:19:08.660
And these three individuals, each one in a different context, had an opportunity to do something.

cue0157414
00:19:09.699 --> 00:19:12.660
And they grabbed it.

cue0157415
00:19:13.699 --> 00:19:20.660
And they forged their own universe.

cue0157416
00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:29.619
So therefore, this, for my mind, is mysticism.

cue0157417
00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.619
It's not only studying books. Of course, we should read.

cue0157418
00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.619
The Jewish people, the Hebrew people.

cue0157419
00:19:38.619 --> 00:19:51.579
But all this reading and all this studying, they should eventually lead to a crossroad.

cue0157420
00:19:52.619 --> 00:19:58.579
The rabbis say something which baffles the mind.

cue0157421
00:19:59.579 --> 00:20:07.540
He says, how are we going to define a young sage?

cue0157422
00:20:09.579 --> 00:20:18.540
A young sage is somebody who is standing at a crossroad.

cue0157423
00:20:20.579 --> 00:20:27.540
Normally, we are objective.

cue0157424
00:20:29.579 --> 00:20:34.540
We follow the standard directions.

cue0157425
00:20:36.579 --> 00:20:39.540
We speak like everybody else.

cue0157426
00:20:40.579 --> 00:20:45.540
Statistics could tell more or less how we are going to behave.

cue0157427
00:20:46.579 --> 00:20:48.540
We are objective.

cue0157428
00:20:49.579 --> 00:20:51.540
They ask us a question.

cue0157429
00:20:52.579 --> 00:20:54.540
They know exactly what we are going to say.

cue0157430
00:20:55.540 --> 00:21:03.500
And therefore, in a sense, we are not we.

cue0157431
00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:12.500
We are the community of an intellectual movement.

cue0157432
00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:16.500
But we are somebody else.

cue0157433
00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:29.459
A young sage, Atal Michaham, is somebody who reached the end of the road.

cue0157434
00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:33.459
And now the road bifurcates.

cue0157435
00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:44.459
And nobody else before him had traded this new course.

cue0157436
00:21:45.459 --> 00:21:54.420
And you have to make a decision which is absolutely personal.

cue0157437
00:21:55.459 --> 00:21:58.420
It is not objective.

cue0157438
00:21:59.459 --> 00:22:02.420
It is subjective.

cue0157439
00:22:03.459 --> 00:22:08.420
Nobody can teach you and tell you what to do.

cue0157440
00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:15.380
Because if somebody tells you what to do, it is not you who is doing it.

cue0157441
00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:25.380
At one moment in your life, you have to cut the umbilical cord.

cue0157442
00:22:26.420 --> 00:22:28.380
Take a chance.

cue0157443
00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:34.380
I may make the greatest mistake in my life.

cue0157444
00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:38.339
But I am going to do it.

cue0157445
00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:43.339
What is going to be the result? I don't know.

cue0157446
00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:54.339
And you go through an uncharted road.

cue0157447
00:22:56.380 --> 00:23:03.339
Now, for my managers, the mysticism of managers is totally different.

cue0157448
00:23:04.380 --> 00:23:06.339
De cabalá mysticism.

cue0157449
00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:08.339
Why?

cue0157450
00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:20.339
For my managers, if you could speak, if you could articulate your mystical experience,

cue0157451
00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:24.339
it is no longer mystical.

cue0157452
00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:31.339
If you could explain it, if you could say why I did what I did,

cue0157453
00:23:31.339 --> 00:23:34.300
or didn't do what I didn't do,

cue0157454
00:23:35.339 --> 00:23:39.300
you are again, you are in the world of rationality,

cue0157455
00:23:40.339 --> 00:23:43.300
and you were afraid to cross the border.

cue0157456
00:23:44.339 --> 00:23:51.300
So for my managers, the most important aspect of mysticism

cue0157457
00:23:52.339 --> 00:23:57.300
is not the content, is not the vision,

cue0157458
00:23:58.300 --> 00:24:02.260
is the idea of being alone.

cue0157459
00:24:03.300 --> 00:24:05.260
My manager has a beautiful description.

cue0157460
00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:09.260
You are in a dense, dark night.

cue0157461
00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:15.260
You look around you, and there is nothing that you could see.

cue0157462
00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:23.260
And you take a decision, and somehow there is a spark.

cue0157463
00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:26.219
And you see something.

cue0157464
00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:32.219
And you see something that is out of this world because you cannot explain it

cue0157465
00:24:33.260 --> 00:24:35.219
in your own words.

cue0157466
00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:40.219
The spark dissipates.

cue0157467
00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:43.219
You are again in the dark.

cue0157468
00:24:44.260 --> 00:24:50.219
But you remember, there was a moment of illumination.

cue0157469
00:24:51.219 --> 00:24:56.180
And that moment of illumination, you became you.

cue0157470
00:24:58.219 --> 00:25:01.180
Let me explain it better.

cue0157471
00:25:02.219 --> 00:25:12.180
For me, the key to Jewish mysticism is in the scripture.

cue0157472
00:25:13.219 --> 00:25:16.180
In the book of Genesis,

cue0157473
00:25:17.180 --> 00:25:21.140
when our patriarch, Jacob,

cue0157474
00:25:23.180 --> 00:25:26.140
flees the Holy Land,

cue0157475
00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:33.140
going to Alam Naharayim, to his uncle, Laban,

cue0157476
00:25:34.180 --> 00:25:37.140
Jewish mysticism, the vision that Jacob had.

cue0157477
00:25:38.180 --> 00:25:43.140
He saw a ladder going all the way up to heaven.

cue0157478
00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:47.099
The ladder standing firmly on earth.

cue0157479
00:25:48.140 --> 00:25:50.099
And lo and behold,

cue0157480
00:25:57.140 --> 00:26:02.099
And behold, the angels of the Lord

cue0157481
00:26:03.140 --> 00:26:07.099
were climbing up the ladder

cue0157482
00:26:08.140 --> 00:26:10.099
and descending the ladder.

cue0157483
00:26:14.140 --> 00:26:16.099
There's a problem.

cue0157484
00:26:17.140 --> 00:26:19.099
There's a problem.

cue0157485
00:26:20.140 --> 00:26:24.099
And all, more or less, including my mothers, give the same answer.

cue0157486
00:26:25.140 --> 00:26:28.099
What kind of angels are we talking about?

cue0157487
00:26:30.140 --> 00:26:33.099
Angels, we imagine,

cue0157488
00:26:35.140 --> 00:26:38.099
they inhabit heaven.

cue0157489
00:26:39.140 --> 00:26:42.099
If they inhabit heaven,

cue0157490
00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:48.099
then the Tora, the truth of God, are first coming down

cue0157491
00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:51.099
and then going up.

cue0157492
00:26:52.140 --> 00:26:54.099
But the scripture doesn't tell you this.

cue0157493
00:26:55.140 --> 00:26:57.099
It tells you the other way around.

cue0157494
00:26:58.140 --> 00:27:02.099
First climb up.

cue0157495
00:27:06.140 --> 00:27:09.099
Even Gavirol says something about it.

cue0157496
00:27:10.099 --> 00:27:13.060
A young contemporary of mine,

cue0157497
00:27:17.099 --> 00:27:20.060
and my mother develops it in the guide.

cue0157498
00:27:22.099 --> 00:27:25.060
The angels of God,

cue0157499
00:27:27.099 --> 00:27:29.060
something useful.

cue0157500
00:27:31.099 --> 00:27:33.060
Something useful.

cue0157501
00:27:35.099 --> 00:27:37.060
And then when you,

cue0157502
00:27:39.099 --> 00:27:41.060
and you benefit

cue0157503
00:27:42.099 --> 00:27:44.060
your people,

cue0157504
00:27:46.099 --> 00:27:49.060
when you translate your vision

cue0157505
00:27:51.099 --> 00:27:55.060
into something that is useful, that is good.

cue0157506
00:27:57.099 --> 00:28:02.060
For my mothers, if you read very carefully the last part of the guide,

cue0157507
00:28:03.099 --> 00:28:06.060
the ultimate purpose

cue0157508
00:28:07.060 --> 00:28:11.020
of mystical vision is hesed.

cue0157509
00:28:12.060 --> 00:28:14.020
To practice

cue0157510
00:28:15.060 --> 00:28:17.020
Gimilut Hasarim.

cue0157511
00:28:19.060 --> 00:28:21.020
Good deeds to people.

cue0157512
00:28:23.060 --> 00:28:25.020
I think that

cue0157513
00:28:26.060 --> 00:28:29.020
if you understand correctly,

cue0157514
00:28:31.060 --> 00:28:33.020
is the chariot.

cue0157515
00:28:33.020 --> 00:28:35.979
You remember the chariot that Ezekiel saw

cue0157516
00:28:38.020 --> 00:28:41.979
as the temple was being destroyed in Jerusalem.

cue0157517
00:28:44.020 --> 00:28:46.979
Ezekiel sees a chariot

cue0157518
00:28:49.020 --> 00:28:52.979
pulled by keruvim, the chariots.

cue0157519
00:28:55.020 --> 00:28:57.979
For my mother, this is the ultimate mysticism.

cue0157520
00:28:58.020 --> 00:28:59.979
There's nothing higher than that.

cue0157521
00:29:00.979 --> 00:29:06.939
He doesn't want to tell us about what is the meaning of this

cue0157522
00:29:07.979 --> 00:29:09.939
because it's forbidden, he said.

cue0157523
00:29:10.979 --> 00:29:13.939
You have to decipher on your own what I mean to say.

cue0157524
00:29:14.979 --> 00:29:16.939
Work your mind.

cue0157525
00:29:18.979 --> 00:29:22.939
But he says two different things.

cue0157526
00:29:23.979 --> 00:29:27.939
First of all, the Merkava, the chariot.

cue0157527
00:29:27.939 --> 00:29:29.900
The chariot

cue0157528
00:29:29.939 --> 00:29:31.900
is the cosmos.

cue0157529
00:29:33.939 --> 00:29:35.900
The universe.

cue0157530
00:29:37.939 --> 00:29:40.900
And somehow this universe

cue0157531
00:29:41.939 --> 00:29:43.900
is being pulled

cue0157532
00:29:44.939 --> 00:29:46.900
by keruvim.

cue0157533
00:29:48.939 --> 00:29:50.900
Now, mind you,

cue0157534
00:29:52.939 --> 00:29:55.900
in Hebrew, you write Cherub,

cue0157535
00:29:56.900 --> 00:30:00.859
Kaf, Resh, Vav, Bet.

cue0157536
00:30:01.900 --> 00:30:03.859
That's the way you write Cherub.

cue0157537
00:30:04.900 --> 00:30:06.859
